--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- free rigid rod (buoyant spar) held by four taut polyester legs, current, dynamic
-- A 10 m, 1.0 m diameter buoyant rigid rod stands upright between z = -30 m (End A) and z = -20 m
-- (End B) in 50 m of water. Its dry mass (300 kg/m) is below its displaced mass (~805 kg/m), so the
-- rod is net buoyant. Two legs run from its lower end (Rod1A) to anchors 25 m upstream and
-- downstream; two legs run from its upper end (Rod1B) to anchors 30 m to either side. Every rod
-- end must carry at least one line. A 0.5 m/s uniform current in +X loads the rod (ROD TYPES
-- Cd/Ca, no end effects CdEnd/CaEnd, CableDyn axial side drag CdAx) and the legs. Rods run on the
-- dynamic EI=0 point-system path, so the deck sets dtM/TMax.
--------------------- LINE TYPES ---------------------------------------
TypeName   Diam     MassDenInAir   EA         BA/-zeta   EI       Cd_n  Cd_t  Ca_n  Ca_t
(-)        (m)      (kg/m)         (N)        (N-s/-)    (N-m^2)  (-)   (-)   (-)   (-)
poly       0.10     10.0           2.0e7      -1.0       0.0      1.2   0.2   1.0   0.0
--------------------- ROD TYPES ----------------------------------------
